nL96: ## Repository navigation\nL97: \nL98:   *   * 【47†Code】\nL99:   * 【48†Issues142 (142)】\nL100:   * 【49†Pull requests】\nL101:   * 【50†Discussions】\nL102:   * 【51†Actions】\nL103:   * 【52†Projects】\nL104:   * 【53†Security and quality】\nL105:   * 【54†Insights】\nL106: \nL107: More items\nL108: \nL109: # Releases: eyalroz/cuda-api-wrappers\nL110: \nL111: 【55†Releases】 【56†Tags】\nL112: \nL113: [Input: Find a release] [Input]\nL114: \nL115: Releases · eyalroz/cuda-api-wrappers\nL116: ## Release list\nL117:   * 【57†Version 0.9.0 Release Candidate 1: Namespace switch, compatibility restoration, many minor changes】\nL118:   * 【58†Version 0.8.2: CUDA 13.1 compatibility, minor additions & bug fixes】\nL119:   * 【59†Version 0.8.1 CUDA 12.x compatibility improvements & minor fixes】\nL120:   * 【60†Version 0.8.0 nvFatbin , CUDA 12.x features, sync-async op unification, static targets etc.】\nL121:   * 【61†Version 0.7.1: Work on unique_span, minor bug fixes and tweaks】\nL122:   * 【62†Version 0.7.0: Graph support】\nL123:   * 【63†Version 0.6.9: Documentation update, unique_span's, bug fixes, many small improvements】\nL124:   * 【64†Version 0.6.8: CUDA 12.x features, launch config builder improvements, etc.】\nL125:   * 【65†Version 0.6.7: Build & compatibility improvements】\nL126:   * 【66†Version 0.6.6: Minor bug fixes + compatibility improvements】\nL127: Jump to release\nL128: ## Version 0.9.0 Release Candidate 1: Namespace switch, compatibility restoration, many minor changes\nL129: \nL130: 【67†Version 0.9.0 Release Candidate 1: Namespace switch, compatibility restoration, many minor changes】\nL131: \nL132: Pre-release\nL133: \nL134: Compare\nL135: \nL136: # Choose a tag to compare\nL137: \nL138: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL139: \nL140: Filter\nL141: \nL142: Loading [Input]\nL143: \nL144: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL145: \nL146: ### Uh oh!\nL147: \nL148: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL149: ## No results found\nL150: \nL151: 【56†View all tags】\nL152: \nL153: 【68†Image: @eyalroz†avatars.githubusercontent.com】 【46†eyalroz】 released this 29 Sep 21:30\nL154: \nL155: 【69†v0.9.0-rc1】\nL156: \nL157: 【70†`ae6dc76`】\nL158: \nL159: Changes since 【71†v0.8.2】:\nL160: \nL161: ## CUDA compatibility\nL162: \nL163: This version is compatible with CUDA versions 9.0 ... 13.4.2 (the latest version as of the time of writing), and builds on Windows with the more recent of these versions. But - please read on.\nL164: ### Namespace change: `cuda::` -> `cuda_::`\nL165: \nL166: Recent CUDA versions have been making more and more use of the `cuda::` namespace - in CUDA APIs, even if you've never including anything from the CCCL library, where this namespace and classes within it are defined. The API headers simply drag in a pile of code from there. That's deplorable, but - I can't prevent that from happening. The result has been increasing clashes with my library, even though I was \"here first\"... and naturally NVIDIA doesn't care.\nL167: So, it is with a heavy heart that I must announce that the namespace for this library has changed from `cuda::` to `cuda_::`. And `cuda::` is for use by NVIDIA. This obviates 【72†#771】 and is the resolution of 【73†#773】. As a result of this, we can drop the underscore from the `detail_` namespace - since we are no longer concerned about clashing with NVIDIA in there; and that's 【74†#805】.\nL168: # Bug fixes\nL169: \nL170:   * 【75†#828】 : Restored compatibility with CUDA 12.1 and earlier\nL171:   * 【76†#816】 : Fixed the invalid r-value constructor in class `optional_ref`\nL172:   * 【77†#811】 : Graph node builder field setter methods now never copy the builder\nL173:   * 【78†#798】 : Correct some `max_shared_memory_per_block()` stats and comments\nL174:   * 【79†#779】 : Fixed scope content ensurance action in `cuda::event::detail::enqueue()`\nL175:   * 【80†#778】 : Fixed a primary context reference counting issue\nL176: # Usability improvements\nL177:   * 【81†#813】 : Now using Martin Moene's 【82†`optional_lite` class】 - a standalone implementation of `optional<T>` supporting pre-C++17 versions of the standard - instead of our \"poor man's span\". (This subsumes issue 【83†#802】, 【84†#803】 resolved before this switch)\nL178:   * 【85†#807】 : External memory `resource_t` class - marked more methods as `noexcept` and add the missing `owning()` method\nL179:   * 【83†#802】, 【86†#806】 : Throwing exceptions in destructors - the code now behaves uniformy, and is controlled by the `CAW_THROW_IN_DESTRUCTORS` preprocessor definition (defined/undefined). Destructors will have their `noexcept` spec defined by `CAW_DESTRUCTOR_EXCEPTION_SPEC` - which is automatically defined based on `CAW_THROW_IN_DESTRUCTORS`\nL180:   * 【87†#804】 : When launching a type-erased kernel with marshalled arguments, in debug mode, now checking for nulls before the argument-terminating null\nL181:   * 【88†#799】 : Named status codes revamp\nL182:   * 【89†#797】 : Some revamping of the `device::properties_t` class\nL183:   * 【90†#780】 : Allow specifying the device when launching a non-wrapped kernel\nL184: ## 'Unsoundness' fixes\nL185:   * 【91†#830】 : Now sanity-checking narrowing cast results\nL186:   * 【92†#826】 : Rename `STRINGIFY` to `CAW_STRINGIFY`\nL187:   * 【93†#822】 : Virtual destructors in child classes of `compilation_output_t`\nL188:   * 【94†#819】 : Now avoiding some `reinterpret_cast()` in memset graph node params building\nL189:   * 【95†#815】 : In graph node builders, avoid copying wrapper class instances and use references and `optional_ref`'s (enabled by 【81†#813】)\nL190:   * 【96†#814】 : Fixed some gaffes in graph node builders: double-copying, misnamed method, redundant const qualifier\nL191:   * 【97†#812】 : Get rid of the `do_()` mechanism in builders\nL192:   * 【98†#809】 : peer-access-related functions taking contexts will now take them by reference, not by value\nL193:   * 【99†#782】 : Now properly assuming created streams don't implicitly synchronize with the default stream\nL194: ## `unique_span` improvements\nL195: \nL196:   * 【100†#783】 : Mark more `unique_span` methods as `noexcept`\nL197:   * 【101†#786】 : Allow calling `make_unique_span()` for device memory from the `cuda::` (now `cuda_::` namespace\nL198:   * 【102†#788】 : Support generating `unique_spas`'s without having to specify their element type\nL199: ## Library build process\nL200: \nL201:   * 【103†#824】 : Can now configure whether or not to throw in destructors via a CMake option\nL202:   * 【104†#776】 : Now dealing with the lack of `nv_decode.h` (which we want...) on Windows\nL203:   * 【105†#775】 : Now associating all header files with the library target (rather than just copying them on installation)\nL204:   * 【106†#774】 : Avoding redundant setting of build target directories\nL205: ## Other changes to the library\nL206:   * 【107†#831】 : `optional_ref::value_or()` is now marked `noexcept\nL207:   * 【108†#829】 : Avoid some GCC 7 warnings\nL208:   * 【109†#827】 : Switched from `namespace module` to `namespace module_` to avoid clashing with the module keyword in newer versions of the C++ standard\nL209:   * 【110†#823】 : No longer need `graph::detail` types when calling `graph::` definitions\nL210:   * 【111†#821】 : Revamped the handle ownership mechanism (using some factored-out utility classes)\nL211:   * 【112†#820】 : Encapsulated the reference unit / ownership holding mechanism for wrapper/proxy classes, into a `token_holder` and `handle_ownership_t` classes. This means that the specialty constructor, destructor and assignment code for almost proxy classes can now be removed entirely, and they are simply defaulted (or deleted, for copy-construction and copy-assignment). This also means that non-copying of proxy classes, which may own anything, is now enforced.\nL212:   * 【113†#817】 Switched the code to use \"east const\" rather than \"const west\", i.e. placing `const` after the type type name rather than before it. This is better for consistency of typing, disambiguation, and multi-line alignment. See 【114†this blog post†hackingcpp.com】 about this matter.\nL213:   * 【115†#800】 : Drop wrapper function for `cudaSetValidDevices()`\nL214:   * 【116†#787】, 【117†#801】 : Redundant syntax removal (namespace, `constexpr const`, `inline` which is implicit)\nL215:   * 【118†#777】 : Naming consistency improvements\nL216:   * 【119†#784】 : Drop some redundant namespace qualifiers\nL217: Assets 2\nL218: \nL219: Loading\nL220: ### Uh oh!\nL221: \nL222: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL223: \nL224: 0 【112†Join discussion】\nL225: \nL226: ## Version 0.8.2: CUDA 13.1 compatibility, minor additions & bug fixes\nL227: \nL228: 【71†Version 0.8.2: CUDA 13.1 compatibility, minor additions & bug fixes】\nL229: \nL230: 【120†Latest】\nL231: \nL232: Compare\nL233: \nL234: # Choose a tag to compare\nL235: \nL236: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL237: \nL238: Filter\nL239: \nL240: Loading [Input]\nL241: \nL242: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL243: \nL244: ### Uh oh!\nL245: \nL246: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL247: ## No results found\nL248: \nL249: 【56†View all tags】\nL250: \nL251: 【68†Image: @eyalroz†avatars.githubusercontent.com】 【46†eyalroz】 released this 10 Nov 10:47\nL252: \nL253: 【121†v0.8.2】\nL254: \nL255: 【122†`c2f2a2b`】\nL256: \nL257: Changes since 【123†v0.8.1】:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReleases · eyalroz/cuda-api-wrappers · GitHub (https://github.com/eyalroz/cuda-api-wrappers/releases)\nciteturn6view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn5view3\",\"pattern\":\"Oct\"}); Total lines: 922\nL779:   * 【295†#585】 You can now write `cuda::memory::make_unique()` - and it's assumed you mean device memory (you have to specify a device or device context though)\nL780:   * 【296†#575】 Moved `apriori_compiled_kernel_t` into the `kernel` namespace, yielding `kernel::apriori_compiled_it`\nL783:   * 【300†#566】 Can now properly get and set properties on kernels (raw functions and handles)\nL784: ## Compatibility\nL785: \nL786:   * 【301†#572】 Fixed broken CUDA 9.x compatibility\nL787: \nL788: Assets 2\nL789: \nL790: Loading\nL791: \nL792: ### Uh oh!\nL793: \nL794: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL795: \nL796: 1 【302†Join discussion】\nL797: \nL798: ## Version 0.6.7: Build & compatibility improvements\nL799: \nL800: 【272†Version 0.6.7: Build & compatibility improvements】\nL801: \nL802: Compare\nL803: \nL804: # Choose a tag to compare\nL805: \nL806: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL807: \nL808: Filter\nL809: \nL810: Loading [Input]\nL811: \nL812: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL813: \nL814: ### Uh oh!\nL815: \nL816: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL817: ## No results found\nL818: \nL819: 【56†View all tags】\nL820: \nL821: 【68†Image: @eyalroz†avatars.githubusercontent.com】 【46†eyalroz】 released this 27 Dec 16:15\nL822: \nL823: 【303†v0.6.7】\nL824: \nL825: 【304†`0246310`】\nL826: \nL827: Changes since 【305†v0.6.6】:\nL828: ## Build process & build configuration changes\nL829:   * 【306†#555】 : No longer enabling any languages when configuring the project - it is not strictly necessary at that point.\nL830:   * 【307†#557】 : Now setting EXPORT_ALL_SYMBOLS as a target property rather than globally (relevant for Windows builds mostly).\nL831:   * 【308†#558】 : Now avoiding incompatibility with CMake 3.25-3.28, by avoiding adding a dependency to a CUDA:: target, and not trying to recreate it if it already exists.\nL832:   * 【309†#562】 Slightly streamlined the package config file (and no longer preprocessing it).\nL833:   * 【310†#563】 Now enabling the C++ language before declaring the dependence (with `find_package()`) on the Threads library.\nL834: ## Compatibility\nL835: \nL836:   * 【311†#506】 : Windows builds no longer fail due to missing `cudaProfiler.h`\nL837:   * 【312†#504】 : Build on Windows should now also succeed when using cooperative groups.\nL838: ## Other changes\nL839: \nL840:   * 【313†#556】 Moved the `CompileWithWarnings.cmake` module into the `examples/` subfolder, which is the only place it's used.\nL841:   * 【314†#561】 Dropped an unused function and method in the launch config builder source code and class, respectively, and added some orphaned validation logic when obtaining the grid and block dimensions, so as not to ignore the overall dimensions.\nL842: \nL843: * * *\nL844:   * Want to help me with testing 0.7? Drop me a line... (it will have CUDA execution graph support)\nL845:   * Have you tried this version and are satisfied with the changes? Thumb-up just below this line to let others know as well.\nL846: \nL847: Assets 2\nL848: \nL849: Loading\nL850: ### Uh oh!\nL851: \nL852: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL853: \nL854: [Input][Input] [Input]\nL855: \nL856: eclipse0922 reacted with thumbs up emoji\nL857: \nL858: All reactions\nL859: \nL860:   * 1 reaction\nL861: \nL862: 1 person reacted\nL863: \nL864: ## Version 0.6.6: Minor bug fixes + compatibility improvements\nL865: \nL866: 【305†Version 0.6.6: Minor bug fixes + compatibility improvements】\nL867: \nL868: Compare\nL869: \nL870: # Choose a tag to compare\nL871: \nL872: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL873: \nL874: Filter\nL875: \nL876: Loading [Input]\nL877: \nL878: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL879: ### Uh oh!\nL880: \nL881: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL882: \nL883: ## No results found\nL884: \nL885: 【56†View all tags】\nL886: \nL887: 【68†Image: @eyalroz†avatars.githubusercontent.com】 【46†eyalroz】 released this 04 Oct 20:27\nL888: \nL889: 【315†v0.6.6】\nL890: \nL891: 【316†`d2d2ad6`】\nL892: \nL893: Changes since 【317†v0.6.4】:\nL894: ## Functionality improvements\nL895: \nL896:   * 【318†#545】 Now checking, and throwing, errors due to `cudaGetLastError()` after kernel launches (mostly grid errors)\nL897:   * 【319†#547】 When compiling in debug mode, now performing more launch configuration validity checks before launching a kernel\nL898:   * 【320†#549】 Avoiding some excessive device property querying.\nL899: ## Bug fixes\nL900:   * 【321†#539】, 【322†#544】 NVRTC compilation logs now returned without a trailing nul (`'\\0'`) character.\nL901:   * 【323†#542】 More robust use of namespace in the library's macros, so they don't trigger compilation errors regardless of the namespace of the code you use them in\nL902:   * 【324†#543】 Now retrieving correct error strings again for Runtime-API-only errors\nL903:   * 【325†#550】 Fixed a wrong side of comparison in some block configuration logic of the launch config builder\nL904:   * 【326†#553】 Replaced inappropriate use of `cbegin()` and `cend()` in favor of `begin()` and `end()` in `rtc::program::add_headers()` code which may take inputs without these two methods.\nL905: ## Compatibility\nL906: \nL907:   * 【327†#546】 Resolved a build on Windows with `rtc.hpp` - fixed an overload resolution issue regarding compilation parameter marshalling.\nL908: \nL909: * * *\nL910: \nL911: Want to help me with testing 0.7? Drop me a line... (it will have CUDA execution graph support)\nL912: \nL913: Assets 2\nL914: \nL915: Loading\nL916: \nL917: ### Uh oh!\nL918: \nL919: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL920: \nL921: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rapidsai/cudf/main/cpp/src/utilities/cuda_memcpy.cu)\nciteturn6view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/plain; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn5view0\",\"pattern\":\"cudaMemcpyBatchAsync\"}); Total lines: 136\nL0: /*\nL1:  * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2024-2026, NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.\nL2:  * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\nL3:  */\nL4: #include <cudf/detail/utilities/cuda.cuh>\nL5: #include <cudf/detail/utilities/cuda_memcpy.hpp